{"abstract":"The Danish Reproducibility Network (DKRN) is a grassroots initiative for establishing a peer-supportive reproducibility-focused academic network in Denmark. We modelled our approach on already existing national Reproducibility Networks. We consulted with researchers and research support professionals to identify the needs of the research community. Three themes emerged around policy implementation, training and the appropriate application of reproducible practices. The network aims to address these three themes in a strategic plan, which harnesses the benefits of grassroots initiatives. The mission of the DKRN is therefore to facilitate communication, peer-support, and the exchange of ideas through a network of topic and geographical nodes. The network is open to researchers and research support professionals from all career stages and disciplines. It aligns with broader international initiatives, and national institutions, positioning itself as a contributor to the Danish research ecosystem.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Topor, Marta","Bonnet, Philippe","Cheplygina, Veronika","Dam, Vibeke Høyrup","Wildgaard, Lorna Elizabeth"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-759596"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Linköping University"],"keyword":["Community building","Open research","Peer support","Reproducible research"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a grassroots approach to peer support by the danish reproducibility network","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djc","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13104-024-06912-7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-759596","identifier":[{"id":"85203448745","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11389419","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"39256756","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-109d0a32-b7e1-44aa-824c-17984597c054"],"keyword":["Community building","Grassroots initiatives","Open research","Peer support","Reproducibility network","Reproducible research"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6BC3693E380E6CC893DED9F2E3D1CC26"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13104-024-06912-7","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/405256227/A_grassroots_approach.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Movement and Neuroscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"linköping university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Linköping University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Marta","key":"toporpau","last":"Topor","locid":"5aeeb227-36ba-45c5-8cfb-76a9c2922b38","name":"Topor, Marta","orcid":"0000-0003-3761-392X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Philippe","key":"bonnetpau","last":"Bonnet","locid":"38554688-0550-450a-9321-98d8b7213716","name":"Bonnet, Philippe","orcid":"0000-0002-0234-5374","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Veronika","key":"cheplyginapau","last":"Cheplygina","name":"Cheplygina, Veronika","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Vibeke Høyrup","key":"dampau","last":"Dam","name":"Dam, Vibeke Høyrup","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lorna","key":"wildgaardpau","last":"Wildgaard","locid":"6e7eb004-dfd6-47b8-aca9-38cb594ceae4","name":"Wildgaard, Lorna Elizabeth","name_org":"Wildgaard, Lorna","orcid":"0000-0002-3900-5058","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39256756"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13104-024-06912-7","issn":["17560500"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Research Notes","paperid":"256","status":"p","title":"BMC Research Notes","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85203448745"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-109d0a32-b7e1-44aa-824c-17984597c054"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A grassroots approach to peer support by the Danish Reproducibility Network","type":"Journal Comment","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-759596","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Medical Imaging (MI) datasets are fundamental to artificial intelligence in healthcare. The accuracy, robustness, and fairness of diagnostic algorithms depend on the data (and its quality) used to train and evaluate the models. MI datasets used to be proprietary, but have become increasingly available to the public, including on community-contributed platforms (CCPs) like Kaggle or HuggingFace. While open data is important to enhance the redistribution of data’s public value, we find that the current CCP governance model fails to uphold the quality needed and recommended practices for sharing, documenting, and evaluating datasets. In this paper, we conduct an analysis of publicly available machine learning datasets on CCPs, discussing datasets’ context, and identifying limitations and gaps in the current CCP landscape. We highlight differences between MI and computer vision datasets, particularly in the potentially harmful downstream effects from poor adoption of recommended dataset management practices. We compare the analyzed datasets across several dimensions, including data sharing, data documentation, and maintenance. We find vague licenses, lack of persistent identifiers and storage, duplicates, and missing metadata, with differences between the platforms. Our research contributes to efforts in responsible data curation and AI algorithms for healthcare.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Jiménez Sánchez, Amelia","Avlona, Natalia-Rozalia","Juodelyte, Dovile","Sourget, Théo","Vang-Larsen, Caroline","Rogers, Anna","Zajac, Hubert Dariusz","Cheplygina, Veronika"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776372"],"event":{"acronym":"NeurIPS","title":"Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Data governance","Datasets","Healthcare","Medical imaging","Open data"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"copycats the many lives of a publicly available medical imaging dataset","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://openreview.net/forum?id=X4KImMSIRq#discussion","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Independent Research Council Denmark (DFF) Inge Lehmann 1134-00017B."],"id":"S01-000.00-776372","ids":["itu-1732a5a6-64e1-44e9-9d36-fe4367fcc30c"],"keyword":["data governance","dataset management","datasets","healthcare","medical imaging","open data"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-642DFED5726C58B113549A53E4408BAB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://openreview.net/forum?id=X4KImMSIRq#discussion","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Amelia","key":"jiménezsánchezpau","last":"Jiménez Sánchez","locid":"64730011-f493-4dbb-abf6-b48924ddc794","name":"Jiménez Sánchez, Amelia","orcid":"0000-0001-7870-0603","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Natalia-Rozalia","key":"avlonapau","last":"Avlona","name":"Avlona, Natalia-Rozalia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dovile","key":"juodelytepau","last":"Juodelyte","locid":"6800c64b-0e54-49cb-a703-384b4987b70c","name":"Juodelyte, Dovile","orcid":"0000-0002-6195-1120","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Théo","key":"sourgetpau","last":"Sourget","locid":"ea2d2480-46fb-493d-8dd4-6f054f58098a","name":"Sourget, Théo","orcid":"0009-0005-0220-9590","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Caroline","key":"vanglarsenpau","last":"Vang-Larsen","name":"Vang-Larsen, Caroline","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"rogerspau","last":"Rogers","locid":"c40e1e8a-50ee-4a7c-b7f0-2fc0fdd62adc","name":"Rogers, Anna","orcid":"0000-0002-4845-4023","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hubert Dariusz","key":"zajacpau","last":"Zajac","name":"Zajac, Hubert Dariusz","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Veronika","key":"cheplyginapau","last":"Cheplygina","locid":"1c4bfd79-4336-4b17-a672-9acb465f15c0","name":"Cheplygina, Veronika","orcid":"0000-0003-0176-9324","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"edition":"2024","status":"p","subtitle":"Datasets and Benchmarks Track","title":"Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems 38 (NeurIPS 2024)","volume":"NeurIPS"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1732a5a6-64e1-44e9-9d36-fe4367fcc30c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Copycats: the many lives of a publicly available medical imaging dataset","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776372","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Medical imaging papers often focus on methodology, but the quality of the algorithms and the validity of the conclusions are highly dependent on the datasets used. As creating datasets requires a lot of effort, researchers often use publicly available datasets, there is however no adopted standard for citing the datasets used in scientific papers, leading to difficulty in tracking dataset usage. In this work, we present two open-source tools we created that could help with the detection of dataset usage, a pipeline1 using OpenAlex and full-text analysis, and a PDF annotation software2 used in our study to manually label the presence of datasets. We applied both tools on a study of the usage of 20 publicly available medical datasets in papers from MICCAI and MIDL. We compute the proportion and the evolution between 2013 and 2023 of 3 types of presence in a paper: cited, mentioned in the full text, cited and mentioned. Our findings demonstrate the concentration of the usage of a limited set of datasets. We also highlight different citing practices, making the automation of tracking difficult.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Sourget, Théo","Akkoç, Ahmet","Winther, Stinna","Lyngbye Galsgaard, Christine","Jiménez Sánchez, Amelia","Juodelyte, Dovile","Petitjean, Caroline","Cheplygina, Veronika"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776403"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Rouen Normandy"],"keyword":["Annotation tools","Bibliometrics","Citations","Datasets","Medical imaging","Meta analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"citation needed data usage and citation practices in medical imaging conferences","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://openreview.net/forum?id=gFIepubv7E","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776403","ids":["itu-647d7ef7-9ed5-414c-92fc-2b2e4968a7c9"],"keyword":["Annotation tools","Bibliometrics","Citations","Data re-use","Datasets","Medical imaging","Meta-analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2A1A0603E721554E11AC56F18DF91F1D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://openreview.net/forum?id=gFIepubv7E","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["ZiteLab ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"fr","key":"university of rouen normandy","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Rouen Normandy","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Théo","key":"sourgetpau","last":"Sourget","locid":"ea2d2480-46fb-493d-8dd4-6f054f58098a","name":"Sourget, Théo","orcid":"0009-0005-0220-9590","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ahmet","key":"akkoçpau","last":"Akkoç","name":"Akkoç, Ahmet","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Stinna","key":"wintherpau","last":"Winther","name":"Winther, Stinna","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Christine","key":"lyngbyegalsgaardpau","last":"Lyngbye Galsgaard","name":"Lyngbye Galsgaard, Christine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Amelia","key":"jiménezsánchezpau","last":"Jiménez Sánchez","locid":"64730011-f493-4dbb-abf6-b48924ddc794","name":"Jiménez Sánchez, Amelia","orcid":"0000-0001-7870-0603","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dovile","key":"juodelytepau","last":"Juodelyte","locid":"6800c64b-0e54-49cb-a703-384b4987b70c","name":"Juodelyte, Dovile","orcid":"0000-0002-6195-1120","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Caroline","key":"petitjeanpau","last":"Petitjean","name":"Petitjean, Caroline","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Veronika","key":"cheplyginapau","last":"Cheplygina","locid":"1c4bfd79-4336-4b17-a672-9acb465f15c0","name":"Cheplygina, Veronika","orcid":"0000-0003-0176-9324","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"1-22","status":"p","title":"Medical Imaging with Deep Learning (MIDL)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","zitelab aps"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-647d7ef7-9ed5-414c-92fc-2b2e4968a7c9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"[Citation needed] Data usage and citation practices in medical imaging conferences","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776403","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Medical Imaging (MI) datasets are fundamental to artificial intelligence in healthcare. The accuracy, robustness, and fairness of diagnostic algorithms depend on the data (and its quality) used to train and evaluate the models. MI datasets used to be proprietary, but have become increasingly available to the public, including on community-contributed platforms (CCPs) like Kaggle or HuggingFace. While open data is important to enhance the redistribution of data's public value, we find that the current CCP governance model fails to uphold the quality needed and recommended practices for sharing, documenting, and evaluating datasets. In this paper, we conduct an analysis of publicly available machine learning datasets on CCPs, discussing datasets' context, and identifying limitations and gaps in the current CCP landscape. We highlight differences between MI and computer vision datasets, particularly in the potentially harmful downstream effects from poor adoption of recommended dataset management practices. We compare the analyzed datasets across several dimensions, including data sharing, data documentation, and maintenance. We find vague licenses, lack of persistent identifiers and storage, duplicates, and missing metadata, with differences between the platforms. Our research contributes to efforts in responsible data curation and AI algorithms for healthcare.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Jiménez-Sánchez, Amelia","Avlona, Natalia Rozalia","Juodelyte, Dovile","Sourget, Théo","Vang-Larsen, Caroline","Rogers, Anna","Zajac, Hubert Dariusz","Cheplygina, Veronika"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-809050"],"event":{"end":"2024-12-15","place":"Vancouver,; BC, ca","start":"2024-12-08","title":"38th Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2024).","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"copycats the many lives of a publicly available medical imaging dataset","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2024/hash/cdbeaeb8a0313940a5752c4ec8838ca6-Abstract-Datasets_and_Benchmarks_Track.html","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-809050","ids":["ku-0ac5afda-3243-4df0-8e3c-952821c1b3d4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-7924FFF3A0B836BA39E4922BD057734A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/437981761/Copycats.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2024/hash/cdbeaeb8a0313940a5752c4ec8838ca6-Abstract-Datasets_and_Benchmarks_Track.html","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Amelia","key":"jiménezsánchezpau","last":"Jiménez-Sánchez","name":"Jiménez-Sánchez, Amelia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Rozalia Natalia","key":"avlonapau","last":"Avlona","locid":"be82e151-8b78-4656-8f1b-78e2bb512e1e","name":"Avlona, Natalia Rozalia","name_org":"Avlona, Rozalia Natalia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dovile","key":"juodelytepau","last":"Juodelyte","name":"Juodelyte, Dovile","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Théo","key":"sourgetpau","last":"Sourget","name":"Sourget, Théo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Caroline","key":"vanglarsenpau","last":"Vang-Larsen","name":"Vang-Larsen, Caroline","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anna","key":"rogerspau","last":"Rogers","name":"Rogers, Anna","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Hubert Dariusz","key":"zajacpau","last":"Zajac","locid":"5b4b2c83-b0ba-4069-8c3a-1459682b8ab6","name":"Zajac, Hubert Dariusz","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Veronika","key":"cheplyginapau","last":"Cheplygina","name":"Cheplygina, Veronika","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["10495258"],"publisher":"NeurIPS Proceedings","series":"Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems","status":"p","title":"38th Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2024) Track on Datasets and Benchmarks."},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105000517744"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0ac5afda-3243-4df0-8e3c-952821c1b3d4"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Copycats: : the many lives of a publicly available medical imaging dataset","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-809050","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Validation metrics are key for tracking scientific progress and bridging the current chasm between artificial intelligence research and its translation into practice. However, increasing evidence shows that, particularly in image analysis, metrics are often chosen inadequately. Although taking into account the individual strengths, weaknesses and limitations of validation metrics is a critical prerequisite to making educated choices, the relevant knowledge is currently scattered and poorly accessible to individual researchers. Based on a multistage Delphi process conducted by a multidisciplinary expert consortium as well as extensive community feedback, the present work provides a reliable and comprehensive common point of access to information on pitfalls related to validation metrics in image analysis. Although focused on biomedical image analysis, the addressed pitfalls generalize across application domains and are categorized according to a newly created, domain-agnostic taxonomy. The work serves to enhance global comprehension of a key topic in image analysis validation.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Reinke, Annika","Maier-Hein, Lena","Tizabi, Minu Dietlinde","Cheplygina, Veronika"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718922"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","German Cancer Research Center","Heidelberg University "],"keyword":["Biological Imaging","Biomedical Image Processing","Challenges","Classification","Computer vision","Detection","Evaluation","Good Scientific Practice","Instance Segmentation","Localization","Medical imaging","Metrics","Pitfalls","Segmentation","Semantic segmentation","Validation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"understanding metric related pitfalls in image analysis validation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2302.01790.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718922","identifier":[{"id":"85184934082","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-d61350fd-b4c8-47c5-9c0c-d79dd8e727eb"],"keyword":["Biological Imaging","Biomedical Image Processing,","Challenges","Classification","Computer Vision","Detection","Good Scientific Practice","Instance Segmentation","Localization","Medical Imaging","Metrics","Pitfalls","Segmentation","Semantic Segmentation","Validation","evaluation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-55960B338205428B675BD79AC548C91E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2302.01790.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"german cancer research center","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"German Cancer Research Center","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"heidelberg university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Heidelberg University ","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Annika","key":"reinkepau","last":"Reinke","name":"Reinke, Annika","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lena","key":"maierheinpau","last":"Maier-Hein","name":"Maier-Hein, Lena","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Minu Dietlinde","key":"tizabipau","last":"Tizabi","name":"Tizabi, Minu Dietlinde","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Veronika","key":"cheplyginapau","last":"Cheplygina","locid":"1c4bfd79-4336-4b17-a672-9acb465f15c0","name":"Cheplygina, Veronika","orcid":"0000-0003-0176-9324","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"]},"sid":["itu-d61350fd-b4c8-47c5-9c0c-d79dd8e727eb"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Understanding metric-related pitfalls in image analysis validation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718922","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, we use spectral analysis to investigate transfer learning and study model sensitivity to frequency shortcuts in medical imaging. By analyzing the power spectrum density of both pre-trained and fine-tuned model gradients, as well as artificially generated frequency shortcuts, we observe notable differences in learning priorities between models pre-trained on natural vs medical images, which generally persist during fine-tuning. We find that when a model's learning priority aligns with the power spectrum density of an artifact, it results in overfitting to that artifact. Based on these observations, we show that source data editing can alter the model's resistance to shortcut learning. ...","author_count":4,"contributors":["Lu, Yucheng","Juodelyte, Dovile","Victor, Jonathan D.","Cheplygina, Veronika"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776460"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cornell University"],"keyword":["Medical imaging","Shortcut Learning","Transfer learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring connections of spectral analysis and transfer learning in medical imaging","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2407.11379","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776460","ids":["itu-f77bf527-2516-4407-8793-12b89de999f9"],"keyword":["Image statistics","Medical imaging","Shortcut learning","Transfer learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-E831ED914F9C98160593D2160ECFECFC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2407.11379","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"cornell university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Cornell University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yucheng","key":"lupau","last":"Lu","locid":"864e737f-8deb-4b43-8403-8edb558e8567","name":"Lu, Yucheng","orcid":"0000-0003-2990-5252","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dovile","key":"juodelytepau","last":"Juodelyte","locid":"6800c64b-0e54-49cb-a703-384b4987b70c","name":"Juodelyte, Dovile","orcid":"0000-0002-6195-1120","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonathan D.","key":"victorpau","last":"Victor","name":"Victor, Jonathan D.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Veronika","key":"cheplyginapau","last":"Cheplygina","locid":"1c4bfd79-4336-4b17-a672-9acb465f15c0","name":"Cheplygina, Veronika","orcid":"0000-0003-0176-9324","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2407.11379","pages":"11","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f77bf527-2516-4407-8793-12b89de999f9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Exploring connections of spectral analysis and transfer learning in medical imaging ...","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776460","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The influence of bias in datasets on the fairness of model predictions is a topic of ongoing research in various fields. We evaluate the performance of skin lesion classification using ResNet-based CNNs, focusing on patient sex variations in training data and three different learning strategies. We present a linear programming method for generating datasets with varying patient sex and class labels, taking into account the correlations between these variables. We evaluated the model performance using three different learning strategies: a single-task model, a reinforcing multi-task model, and an adversarial learning scheme. Our observations include: 1) sex-specific training data yields better results, 2) single-task models exhibit sex bias, 3) the reinforcement approach does not remove sex bias, 4) the adversarial model eliminates sex bias in cases involving only female patients, and 5) datasets that include male patients enhance model performance for the male subgroup, even when female patients are the majority. To generalise these findings, in future research, we will examine more demographic attributes, like age, and other possibly confounding factors, such as skin colour and artefacts in the skin lesions. We make all code available on Github.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Raumanns, Ralf","Schouten, Gerard","Pluim, Josien P.W.","Cheplygina, Veronika"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776439"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Eindhoven University of Technology","Fontys University of Applied Sciences"],"keyword":["Adversarial learning","Bias","Fairness","Multi task learning","Skin lesions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dataset distribution impacts model fairness single vs multi task learning","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2407.17543","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776439","ids":["itu-ad7aea0e-1b0f-4a0a-8778-01104bc66c8a"],"keyword":["Adversarial learning","Bias","Fairness","Multi-task learning","Skin lesions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3BD1B5588B8E464C7F7CC8D4A7790797"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2407.17543","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"fontys university of applied sciences","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Fontys University of Applied Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"eindhoven university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Eindhoven University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ralf","key":"raumannspau","last":"Raumanns","name":"Raumanns, Ralf","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Gerard","key":"schoutenpau","last":"Schouten","name":"Schouten, Gerard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Josien P.W.","key":"pluimpau","last":"Pluim","name":"Pluim, Josien P.W.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Veronika","key":"cheplyginapau","last":"Cheplygina","locid":"1c4bfd79-4336-4b17-a672-9acb465f15c0","name":"Cheplygina, Veronika","orcid":"0000-0003-0176-9324","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"edition":"15198","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"MICCAI Workshop on Fairness of AI in Medical Imaging (MICCAI FAIMI)","volume":"LNCS"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ad7aea0e-1b0f-4a0a-8778-01104bc66c8a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Dataset Distribution Impacts Model Fairness: Single Vs. Multi-task Learning","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776439","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The availability of large public datasets and the increased amount of computing power have shifted the interest of the medical community to high-performance algorithms. However, little attention is paid to the quality of the data and their annotations. High performance on benchmark datasets may be reported without considering possible shortcuts or artifacts in the data, besides, models are not tested on subpopulation groups. With this work, we aim to raise awareness about shortcuts problems. We validate previous findings, and present a case study on chest X-rays using two publicly available datasets. We share annotations for a subset of pneumothorax images with drains. We conclude with general recommendations for medical image classification.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Jiménez Sánchez, Amelia","Juodelyte, Dovile","Chamberlain, Bethany","Cheplygina, Veronika"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384697"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bias","Chest X ray","Fairness","Metadata","Pneumothorax","Reproducibility","Shortcuts","Validation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"detecting shortcuts in medical images a case study in chest x rays","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ISBI53787.2023.10230572","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This project has received funding from the Independent Research Fund Denmark - Inge Lehmann number 1134-00017B."],"id":"S01-000.00-384697","identifier":[{"id":"85172099640","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e8acb255-4527-4e9b-90e7-38d3c7feda56"],"keyword":["Chest X-ray","Metadata","bias","fairness","pneumothorax","reproducibility","shortcuts","validation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-EF5A3D7B1E3863C6937A7CA5218DED6F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ISBI53787.2023.10230572","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2211.04279.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Amelia","key":"jiménezsánchezpau","last":"Jiménez Sánchez","locid":"64730011-f493-4dbb-abf6-b48924ddc794","name":"Jiménez Sánchez, Amelia","orcid":"0000-0001-7870-0603","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dovile","key":"juodelytepau","last":"Juodelyte","locid":"6800c64b-0e54-49cb-a703-384b4987b70c","name":"Juodelyte, Dovile","orcid":"0000-0002-6195-1120","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bethany","key":"chamberlainpau","last":"Chamberlain","name":"Chamberlain, Bethany","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Veronika","key":"cheplyginapau","last":"Cheplygina","locid":"1c4bfd79-4336-4b17-a672-9acb465f15c0","name":"Cheplygina, Veronika","orcid":"0000-0003-0176-9324","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e8acb255-4527-4e9b-90e7-38d3c7feda56"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Detecting Shortcuts in Medical Images — A Case Study in Chest X-rays","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384697","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Failure is an integral part of life and by extension academia. At the same time, failure is often ignored, with potentially negative consequences both for the science and the scientists involved. This article provides several strategies for learning from and dealing with failure instead of ignoring it. Hopefully, our recommendations are widely applicable, while still taking into account individual differences between academics. These simple rules allow academics to further develop their own strategies for failing successfully in academia.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Gaillard, Stefan","van Viegen, Tara","Veldsman, Michele","Stefan, Melanie","Cheplygina, Veronika"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-712508"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Edinburgh"],"keyword":["Careers","Human learning","Mental health and psychiatry","Peer review","Scientists","Social media","Supervisors","Twitter"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ten simple rules for failing successfully in academia","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://journals.plos.org/ploscompbiol/article/file?id=10.1371/journal.pcbi.1010538&type=printable","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-712508","ids":["itu-302c95fe-9bb4-477d-9121-a99d9304ab2d"],"keyword":["Careers","Human learning","Mental health and psychiatry","Peer review","Scientists","Social media","Supervisors","Twitter"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-185FCA7560DC30E12B93656E25875416"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://journals.plos.org/ploscompbiol/article?id=10.1371/journal.pcbi.1010538","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://journals.plos.org/ploscompbiol/article/file?id=10.1371/journal.pcbi.1010538&type=printable","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of edinburgh","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Edinburgh","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefan","key":"gaillardpau","last":"Gaillard","name":"Gaillard, Stefan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Tara","key":"vanviegenpau","last":"van Viegen","name":"van Viegen, Tara","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Michele","key":"veldsmanpau","last":"Veldsman","name":"Veldsman, Michele","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Melanie","key":"stefanpau","last":"Stefan","name":"Stefan, Melanie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Veronika","key":"cheplyginapau","last":"Cheplygina","locid":"1c4bfd79-4336-4b17-a672-9acb465f15c0","name":"Cheplygina, Veronika","orcid":"0000-0003-0176-9324","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["1553734X","15537358"],"issn_org":["1553734X"],"journal":"PLOS Computational Biology","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS Computational Biology","title_org":"PLoS Computational Biology"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85144239126"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-302c95fe-9bb4-477d-9121-a99d9304ab2d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Ten simple rules for failing successfully in academia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-712508","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"While a key component to the success of deep learning is the availability of massive amounts of training data, medical image datasets are often limited in diversity and size. Transfer learning has the potential to bridge the gap between related yet different domains. For medical applications, however, it remains unclear whether it is more beneficial to pre-train on natural or medical images. We aim to shed light on this problem by comparing initialization on ImageNet and RadImageNet on seven medical classification tasks. Our work includes a replication study, which yields results contrary to previously published findings. In our experiments, ResNet50 models pre-trained on ImageNet tend to outperform those trained on RadImageNet. To gain further insights, we investigate the learned representations using Canonical Correlation Analysis (CCA) and compare the predictions of the different models. Our results indicate that, contrary to intuition, ImageNet and RadImageNet may converge to distinct intermediate representations, which appear to diverge further during fine-tuning. Despite these distinct representations, the predictions of the models remain similar. Our findings show that the similarity between networks before and after fine-tuning does not correlate with performance gains, suggesting that the advantages of transfer learning might not solely originate from the reuse of features in the early layers of a convolutional neural network.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Juodelyte, Dovile","Jiménez Sánchez, Amelia","Cheplygina, Veronika"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-712503"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Medical imaging","Transfer learning","hidden representations","representations learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"revisiting hidden representations in transfer learning for medical imaging","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2302.08272.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This project has been granted funding by the Novo Nordisk Foundation under the agreement number NNF21OC0068816."],"id":"S01-000.00-712503","identifier":[{"id":"86000077157","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-263bd8e8-e131-4fd1-892c-ca18f8175ec7"],"keyword":["Medical imaging","hidden representations","representations learning","transfer learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-D70CFF9A2E69C9E90B7AE7208D16F9E1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2302.08272.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dovile","key":"juodelytepau","last":"Juodelyte","locid":"6800c64b-0e54-49cb-a703-384b4987b70c","name":"Juodelyte, Dovile","orcid":"0000-0002-6195-1120","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Amelia","key":"jiménezsánchezpau","last":"Jiménez Sánchez","locid":"64730011-f493-4dbb-abf6-b48924ddc794","name":"Jiménez Sánchez, Amelia","orcid":"0000-0001-7870-0603","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Veronika","key":"cheplyginapau","last":"Cheplygina","locid":"1c4bfd79-4336-4b17-a672-9acb465f15c0","name":"Cheplygina, Veronika","orcid":"0000-0003-0176-9324","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["28358856"],"journal":"Transactions on Machine Learning Research","status":"p","title":"Transactions on Machine Learning Research"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-86000077157"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-263bd8e8-e131-4fd1-892c-ca18f8175ec7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Revisiting Hidden Representations in Transfer Learning for Medical Imaging","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-712503","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"International benchmarking competitions have become fundamental for the comparative performance assessment of image analysis methods. However, little attention has been given to investigating what can be learnt from these competitions. Do they really generate scientific progress? What are common and successful participation strategies? What makes a solution superior to a competing method? To address this gap in the literature, we performed a multi- center study with all 80 competitions that were conducted in the scope of IEEE ISBI 2021 and MICCAI 2021. Statistical analyses performed based on comprehensive descriptions of the submitted algorithms linked to their rank as well as the underlying participation strategies revealed common char- acteristics of winning solutions. These typically include the use of multi-task learning (63%) and/or multi-stage pipelines (61%), and a focus on augmentation (100%), im- age preprocessing (97%), data curation (79%), and post- processing (66%). The “typical” lead of a winning team is a computer scientist with a doctoral degree, five years of experience in biomedical image analysis, and four years of experience in deep learning. Two core general development strategies stood out for highly-ranked teams: the reflection of the metrics in the method design and the focus on analyz- ing and handling failure cases. According to the organizers, 43% of the winning algorithms exceeded the state of the art but only 11% completely solved the respective domain prob- lem. The insights of our study could help researchers (1) improve algorithm development strategies when approach- ing new problems, and (2) focus on open research questions revealed by this work.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Eisenmann, Matthias","Reinke, Annika","Weru, Vivienn","Tizabi, Minu Dietlinde","Isensee, Fabian","Adler, Tim J.","Ali, Sharib","Andrearczyk, Vincent","Aubreville, Marc","Baid, Ujjwal","Bakas, Spyridon","Balu, Niranjan","Bano, Sophia","Bernal, Jorge","Bodenstedt, Sebastian","Casella, Alessandro","Cheplygina, Veronika"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718928"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Italy","Spain","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","German Cancer Research Center","HES-SO Valais-Wallis","National Center for Tumor Diseases","Polytechnic University of Milan","Technische Hochschule Ingolstadt","University College London - Institute of Education","University of Leeds","University of Murcia","University of Pennsylvania","University of Washington"],"keyword":["Algorithm development strategies","Biomedical image analysis","Comparative performance assessment","Competition participation strategies","Data augmentation","Deep learning experience","Failure case analysis","Image analysis methods","International benchmarking competitions","Multi stage pipelines","Multi task learning","Post processing","Preprocessing","Scientific progress in image analysis","State of the art"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"why is the winner the best","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2303.17719","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718928","ids":["itu-e0d2c492-ca5b-457c-afd9-74d210ab69f6"],"keyword":["\"State of the art\"","Algorithm development strategies","Biomedical image analysis","Comparative performance assessment","Competition participation strategies","Data augmentation","Deep learning experience","Failure case analysis","Image analysis methods","International benchmarking competitions","Multi-sta